{
  "manifest": {
    "activation": [
      "onTransform"
    ],
    "contributes": {
      "settings": [
        {
          "anchor": "snippets.after",
          "description": "Say a trigger and Grain opens its websites and apps, then removes the trigger from your text.",
          "fields": [
            {
              "key": "trigger",
              "kind": "string",
              "label": "Trigger"
            },
            {
              "fields": [
                {
                  "key": "url",
                  "kind": "url",
                  "label": "URL"
                }
              ],
              "itemLabel": "website",
              "key": "websites",
              "kind": "list",
              "label": "Websites"
            },
            {
              "fields": [
                {
                  "key": "path",
                  "kind": "app_path",
                  "label": "App"
                }
              ],
              "itemLabel": "app",
              "key": "apps",
              "kind": "list",
              "label": "Apps"
            }
          ],
          "itemLabel": "action",
          "key": "actions",
          "kind": "list",
          "label": "",
          "order": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    "description": "Say a trigger word to open apps and websites, then have it stripped from what gets pasted. Its settings render right inside the Snippets tab — no separate window. A worked example of the transform hook, the open:url / open:app capabilities, and the reusable declarative list UI.",
    "entry_source": "// Voice Actions — the worker. Runs on the finalized transcript: matches the\r\n// user's configured triggers, opens their websites/apps, and returns the text\r\n// with the trigger removed.\r\n//\r\n// Config lives in the extension's declared settings (rendered natively in the\r\n// Snippets tab — no webview): `actions` is a list of\r\n//   { trigger, websites: [{ url }], apps: [{ path }] }.\r\n//\r\n// Security: this worker never launches anything on its own. `grain.open.url` is\r\n// scheme-allowlisted by the host; `grain.open.app` only launches an app the user\r\n// picked via the app-path control (which records approval). It merely relays the\r\n// user's configured rules.\r\n\r\nfunction normalize(s) {\r\n  return String(s || \"\").toLowerCase().trim();\r\n}\r\n\r\ngrain.onTransform(function (text) {\r\n  return grain.settings.get(\"actions\").then(function (actions) {\r\n    actions = Array.isArray(actions) ? actions : [];\r\n    if (!actions.length) return text;\r\n\r\n    var out = text;\r\n    var fired = [];\r\n    actions.forEach(function (a) {\r\n      var trigger = normalize(a && a.trigger);\r\n      if (!trigger) return;\r\n      var idx = out.toLowerCase().indexOf(trigger);\r\n      if (idx !== -1) {\r\n        out = out.slice(0, idx) + out.slice(idx + trigger.length);\r\n        fired.push(a);\r\n      }\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    // Fire-and-forget so a slow launch never blocks the paste path.\r\n    fired.forEach(function (a) {\r\n      (a.websites || []).forEach(function (w) {\r\n        if (w && w.url) {\r\n          try { grain.open.url(String(w.url)); } catch (e) {}\r\n        }\r\n      });\r\n      (a.apps || []).forEach(function (p) {\r\n        if (p && p.path) {\r\n          try { grain.open.app(String(p.path)); } catch (e) {}\r\n        }\r\n      });\r\n    });\r\n\r\n    return out.replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\r\n  });\r\n});\r\n",
    "grainApi": "^1.0",
    "id": "grain.voice-actions",
    "name": "Voice Actions",
    "permissions": [
      "transform:transcript",
      "open:url",
      "open:app",
      "settings"
    ],
    "repository": "https://github.com/Punit-Dethe/Grain-Extention",
    "tier": "scripted",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "payloads": {}
}
